    {
      "name": "ke_mesh_component",
      "doc": "Renders a mesh with a material. \u0060mesh\u0060/\u0060material\u0060 double as output: the native \u0022render.mesh.resolve\u0022 system (KE_PHASE_UPDATE, src/zig/render/service/src/mesh_resolve.zig) fills them whenever \u0060primitive\u0060 names a known shape and/or the surface fields below have not already resolved to a valid handle. A caller holding real handles just writes them and leaves \u0060primitive\u0060 empty \u2014 the resolve system only acts where a handle is still invalid, so the two paths never conflict.",
